{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cd3gkFjTFcbrLKvymv5fz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Session complete. Summary of what landed:\n\n## WI-171 — rearm the shared-failure page (the declared Next action)\n`agent_route.escalate()` summed strong-tier `CHANGES-REQUESTED` rounds over the **entire** coordinator run, so once the tally hit `page_top_tier_fails` (2), every later review round — even a clean APPROVE — re-paged forever (the exact bleed the 094 design-check traced).\n- Added a `fails_since` index to `escalate()` (default `0` preserves the whole-run count for un-updated callers); `top_tier_fails` now counts only `rounds[fails_since:]`.\n- The coordinator (`agent_loop.py`) advances `page_fails_since = len(rounds)` on **every** page dispatch, so only **new** strong-tier fails after the last dispatch re-page. The last-round tripwire and two-round contradiction windows were already bounded — untouched.\n- Regression test: two fails page → boundary advances → a later APPROVE does **not** page → two fresh fails re-page.\n\n## WI-174 — check_docs multi-backtick fix (a blocker I discovered running WI-171)\nThe commit bar surfaced a **pre-existing** red: `check_docs --stale` reported 3 broken links — all `[...](x.md)` link syntax **quoted as examples** inside double-backtick code spans in review prose (`093-REVIEW-A.md`, committed via a bar-bypassing telemetry commit, + the untracked `094-DESIGN-CHECK.md`). `INLINE_CODE_RE` only stripped single-backtick spans, so the double-backtick run mis-split and leaked a phantom `[](x.md)`. Widened the regex to match an N-backtick run closed by exactly N (CommonMark). **Broken links 3 → 0.** Filed as new scope (`BuildTier=quick`) since it needed a WI.\n\n## Gates (real output)\n- Full suite: **755 passed, 34 skipped in 75.29s**\n- Commit bar: `pytest -m smoke` → **628 passed, 2 skipped**; `check_docs --stale` → **OK, 0 broken** (40 orphan warnings are warn-only)\n- Pre-commit hook floor (arch-map, okf, trajectory-map, trajectory, registry-integrity, derived-gate, skills-sync, format, privacy) — **all PASS** on each of 3 commits. `ruff` reformatted `agent_route.py` (slice spacing).\n\n## Handoff\n- 3 logical commits on `derived-gate-model`; also landed the 094 design-check ruling + its queue residue. **Not pushed** (`push-policy: human`).\n- `docs/run-state` = **RUNNING** (work remains). `docs/next-wi` → **WI-172;WI-173** (the dev-slice batch, one review round, `medium` pin), then **WI-153** resumes the research-knowledge campaign.\n- Note carried forward in status.md/next-wi: the rearm takes effect only on the **next coordinator restart** (routing referees import at process start), so until then successor design-checks still take the **094 fast path**.\n\nNo spine change (SN=24 SR=56 LLR=57 TC=57, orphans=0); both WIs off-spine. Only deferred main-decomposition (WI-080→WI-081) stays parked."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":357,"cache_read_input_tokens":187094,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":357},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6f1cbeab-fafe-447f-adcf-9ad95327441e","uuid":"dcbf54f5-a6da-4142-af92-4115c5870d95","request_id":"req_011Cd3gkEBBvbwr986U8yGxU"}
